'''''Begonia minor''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Begoniaceae]], native to [[Jamaica]]. It's also been introduced to [[Madeira]], [[Réunion]], and the [[Society Islands]].<ref name="KEW" >{{cite web |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:105214-1 |title=''Begonia minor'' Jacq. |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=6 December 2025}}</ref> In 1777, it was the first Begonia to be introduced to Great Britain. Initially, this specimen was known as ''B.&nbsp;nitida.'' "Nitida" means "shining leaves".<ref name="BH">{{cite journal |last1=Kelly |first1=C.M. |title=BEGONIA HISTORY |journal=The Begonian |date=February 1934 |volume=1 |issue=2 |pages=3 |url=https://www.begonias.org/wp-content/uploads/_pda/2021/12/1934.pdf |access-date=1 January 2026 |ref=1934}}</ref> 

''B. minor'' has a [[Begonia#Cultivar_groups|shrub-like]] growing habit, and produces masses of pink flowers year-round. When planted in gardens, it can grow to be {{Convert|3|ft|sigfig=1}} or more in size.<ref name="Sharp">{{cite book |last1=Sharp |first1=Peter G. |url=https://www.ibegonias.filemakerstudio.com.au/PeterSharp/DownToEarthWithBegonias.pdf |title=Down To Earth - With Begonias |year=2011 |pages=16,85 |access-date=6 December 2025}}</ref>

